# Toolchain & Project Structure

## Language

**C11** (`-std=c11`). **No C++.**

## Compiler flags (from `Makefile`)

```
-std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror
-D_XOPEN_SOURCE=700
-Iinclude
-O2          # release (CFLAGS)
```

When the POSIX header probe fails, the Makefile also adds:

```
-DLS_TOTO_WIN32_FS   # FindFirstFileA / GetFileAttributesExA (kernel32, linked by default)
```

No extra `LDFLAGS` are needed on either path.

Debug target uses `CFLAGS_DEBUG`: `-g -O1 -fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer`.

## Artefact layout

All build outputs live under **`build/`**; never write binaries at the repo root
or into `tests/`.

| Artefact | Path |
|----------|------|
| Release binary | `build/ls-toto` (`.exe` on Windows) |
| Debug binary | `build/ls-toto-debug` |
| Main objects | `build/*.o` (from `src/*.c`) |
| Test binary | `build/tests/test_core` |
| Test objects | `build/tests/*.o` (from `tests/*.c` and the linked pure modules) |

`build/.gitkeep` and `build/tests/.gitkeep` keep the directories in git when empty.
`make clean` removes objects and binaries but leaves the `.gitkeep` files.

## Compiler selection

`Makefile` picks **gcc** if available, else **clang**:

```makefile
CC := $(shell command -v gcc >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo gcc || echo clang)
```

On **`OS=Windows_NT`**, if `C:/msys64/ucrt64/bin/gcc` exists, it becomes `CC`
(so Git Bash does not use a minimal MinGW without POSIX headers).

## Platform probe (POSIX headers)

Before compiling, the Makefile preprocesses a snippet containing:

```c
#include <dirent.h>
#include <sys/stat.h>
#include <pwd.h>
#include <grp.h>
```

- **Probe succeeds** → POSIX filesystem path in `ls_toto_fs.c`; all unit tests run.
- **Probe fails** (any header missing) → `-DLS_TOTO_WIN32_FS`; POSIX-only tests `SKIP`.

Typical outcomes:

| Environment | Probe | Filesystem path |
|-------------|-------|-----------------|
| Linux / WSL | success | `opendir`/`readdir`, `lstat`, `getpwuid`/`getgrgid` |
| MSYS2 UCRT64 with full gcc | fail* | `FindFirstFileA` / `GetFileAttributesExA` |
| Git Bash (minimal MinGW) | fail | `FindFirstFileA` / `GetFileAttributesExA` |

\*MinGW-w64 ships `dirent.h` and `sys/stat.h` but not `pwd.h` / `grp.h`, so
native Windows builds take the Win32 path; Cygwin / MSYS-runtime toolchains
with the full POSIX headers keep the POSIX path.

## Build system

**GNU Make** at repo root. Object files are compiled into `build/` and
`build/tests/`, then linked.

| Target | Output |
|--------|--------|
| `make` / `all` | `build/ls-toto` |
| `make debug` | `build/ls-toto-debug` |
| `make test` | builds + runs `build/tests/test_core` |
| `make clean` | removes objects/binaries under `build/` (keeps `.gitkeep`) |
| `make install` | `install -m 755 build/ls-toto /usr/local/bin` (Linux/macOS) |

**Main sources:** `src/main.c`, `src/ls_toto_cli.c`, `src/ls_toto_emit.c`,
`src/ls_toto_fs.c`, `src/ls_toto_sort.c`, `src/ls_toto_format.c`,
`src/ls_toto_out.c`, `src/ls_toto_list.c`

**Test sources (`TEST_SRCS`):** `tests/test_runner.c`, `tests/test_out_stub.c`,
`tests/test_cli_parse.c`, `tests/test_sort_order.c`, `tests/test_format_mode.c`,
`tests/test_format_size.c`, `tests/test_fs_readdir.c`

**Linked pure modules (`TEST_LINKED_SRCS`):** `src/ls_toto_cli.c`,
`src/ls_toto_sort.c`, `src/ls_toto_format.c`

## Dependencies

- **POSIX builds:** libc only (`dirent.h`, `sys/stat.h`, `pwd.h`, `grp.h`,
  `unistd.h`, `time.h`).
- **Win32 filesystem builds:** libc + **kernel32** (`FindFirstFileA`,
  `FindNextFileA`, `GetFileAttributesExA`; linked by default by MinGW).

